<title>BELGIUM: EU will try to be tougher on state aid - Van Miert.</title>
<headline>EU will try to be tougher on state aid - Van Miert.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Competition Commissioner Karel van Miert said on Wednesday the European Commission would try to be tougher dealing with state aid to European industries.</p>
<p>Van Miert said new EU figures showed 97 billion European currencies units had been paid in state aid in the then-12 nation bloc in 1993-94.</p>
<p>Asked what he planned to do about such amounts, he told a news conference: &quot;Try to be even tougher than we have been.&quot;</p>
<p>The Commission is responsible for vetting state aid to make sure it does not harm competition in the EU.</p>
</text>
